The condition $\Gamma^\mu_{
u\lambda} = 0$ indicates that the components of the Levi-Civita connection vanish in a given coordinate chart. In general relativity and differential geometry, this implies that partial derivatives coincide with covariant derivatives ($\ abla_\lambda = \partial_\lambda$) on tensor fields. Globally, this occurs across a manifold if and only if the Riemann curvature tensor vanishes ($R^\mu_{
